WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.180
<v ->So, another quick lecture,</v>

2
00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.140
but this time on RDS-Security,

3
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.150
that you hopefully should know,

4
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.270
but maybe there's a thing or two that you'll learn here.

5
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.590
So you can get KMS encryption at rest

6
00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.040
for your underlying EBS volume and snapshots.

7
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.270
You have the option

8
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:16.350
to use something called TDE, Transparent Data Encryption,

9
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.800
if you have an Oracle or SQL Server database,

10
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.480
managed by RDS.

11
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.110
And you are able to define in-flight encryption,

12
00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.490
SSL encryption, for all the databases.

13
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.620
You are able to use IAM authentication

14
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.810
for MySQL, PostgreSQL and MariaDB,

15
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.320
but that's just for the authentication,

16
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.860
the authorization itself

17
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.350
still happens within RDS, not in IAM.

18
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.670
But still, it's good for user management

19
00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.810
to be done through IAM.

20
00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.890
You can copy an un-encrypted RDS snapshot

21
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:46.750
into an encrypted one,

22
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.010
this is a very common DevOps feature to do,

23
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.270
and CloudTrail cannot be used

24
00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.380
to track queries made within RDS.

25
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.950
You will need to have specific monitoring tools,

26
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.880
for RDS and database security

27
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.130
to get these kind of logs, okay?

28
00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:03.040
So just a very short lecture, to be honest.

29
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.780
We'll have a more deep dive into RDS in another section,

30
00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.160
but here you need to remember

31
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.050
all the security options for RDS,

32
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.740
because the exam may trick you into thinking

33
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.530
TDE is for MySQL,

34
00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.220
or IAM authentication is for Oracle, okay?

35
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:16.053
So that's it.

36
00:01:16.053 --> 00:01:17.680
I will see you in the next lecture.

